/-!
# Compatibility of the fixed common-image lifts

The two native common lifts commute and their product is first-class.
A checked word calculation identifies their product with the third
first-class lift times kernel mask 346. That mask is a displacement of
the third image, so multiplication by it is actual kernel conjugation.
The packed products reuse the existing ATLAS word certificates.
Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Section 2.1, p.489.
-/
